LOFI2 (lofi2) for the Elektron Octatrack MKI / MKII

LOFI2 was written by Bryan T (Bryan Tysinger, https://github.com/bryantysinger)
and contributed to the octabam project, where it was merged as pull request 657
(commit a6f41a1dff922be622e2e8a7d93bc5a5958c90ab); this copy is that module with his
pull request 704, merged 13 October 2026, his SHIFT fix of 14 October 2026
(commit 153063d85cfe13884f0a18394eb9b4917d650dca) and his SHIFT feedback cap,
pull request 843, merged 21 October 2026, as on octabam main at
commit 7795adf0dff8c650968ff53ab5ab47babaf00ffe. It is distributed under
octabam's MIT License, whose full text follows unchanged and is also kept
byte for byte at upstream/LICENSE.

- The module (lofi2.asm, its tables and declaration in manifest.py, the
  render gate verify_lofi2.py, upstream/modules/lofi2/README.md): Bryan T.
- The octabam SDK, schema and harness it is written against: Sam Banks.
- Modwerk's adaptations of manifest.py and verify_lofi2.py (listed in
  README.md and sdk/imports/lofi2-7795adf.json), README.md, TESTING.md,
  octamod.module.json, media/ and presentation/thumbnail.svg are contributed
  under the same MIT terms.

No Elektron firmware, extracted stock routine or table is included. Stock
LO-FI's rates and curve are reproduced from measurements by the author, as
formulas in manifest.py.

